lesson: 216
title: Legs on tables and chairs
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: An ordinary chair stands on 4 legs, and an ordinary table stands on 4 legs too.
explain: So every table and every chair gives 4 legs: count the pieces of furniture, then take 4 for each.
explain: 3 tables and 12 chairs: 3 + 12 = 15 pieces, and 15 × 4 = 60 legs.
vars: a=name t=2..6 c=4..24 z=2..9
answer: (t + c) * 4
exercise: The dining room has {t} tables and {c} chairs. How many furniture legs are in the room?
exercise: {a}'s classroom has {t} tables and {c} chairs. How many legs do the tables and chairs have altogether?
exercise: A café puts out {t} tables and {c} chairs on the pavement. How many legs touch the pavement?
exercise: {a} helps to stack {c} chairs and {t} tables after the school concert. How many legs does the pile have?
exercise: How many legs are there on {t} kitchen tables and {c} chairs?
exercise: In the library there are {t} reading tables and {c} chairs around them. Count the legs of the furniture.
exercise: {t} tables {c} chairs, how many legs. furniture legs not ppl lol
exercise: hall for the party: {t} tables, {c} chairs. legs?
exercise: {a} has to put felt pads on every leg — {t} tables n {c+1} chairs, no wait {c} chairs. how many pads
exercise: my bro says a table has 3 legs. nah, normal ones. {t} tables n {c} chairs, how many legs
exercise: {z} kids sat down but forget them — {t} tables, {c} chairs, how many legs on the furniture
test: Felt pads go on every leg of {c} chairs and {t} tables. How many pads are needed?
test: How many legs stand on the floor of a room with {c} chairs and {t} tables?
test: The canteen has {t} tables, each with chairs; {c} chairs in all. What is the total number of legs of the tables and chairs?
test: {c} chairs + {t} tables, legs?
test: we hired {t} tables and {c} chairs for nan's birthday, {z} balloons too. how many legs on the furniture
test: {a} counts the furniture legs at the café: {t} tables and {c} chairs. What number does {a.he} get?
exam: A refectory is furnished with {t} tables and {c} chairs of conventional construction. Determine the aggregate number of legs upon which the said furniture stands.
exam: Given that {t.words} tables and {c.words} chairs are to be fitted with one protective pad per leg, ascertain the number of pads required.
exam: Compute the total number of furniture legs in an assembly hall containing {c} chairs and {t} tables.
exam: Whereas a library accommodates {t} tables and {c} chairs, state the number of legs belonging to the said items.
exercise: The café "downsized" and sold {z} of its tables. Now {t} tables and {c} chairs are left. How many legs do they stand on?
exercise: bloody removal men "mislaid" {z} chairs, only {t} tables n {c} chairs turned up. how many legs then
test: After Great-Aunt May passed away, the family kept one table for themselves and gave her other {t} tables and {c} chairs to the school. How many furniture legs does the school get?
